From: Morgan Lee <morgan.lee@hangs-cs.example>
To: Tax preparation <tax@finance-demo.example>
Subject: HANGS Construction Services 2026 estimated tax, December payment
Date: Tue, 03 Nov 2026 16:10:00 -0800
Message-ID: <HCS-2026-ES@hangs-cs.example>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="=_HCS_2026_ES_request"

--=_HCS_2026_ES_request
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi,

The December 15 estimate is coming up and I want to get it right this time. S=
o far this year we have paid what we paid each quarter last year: $12,075.00 =
in April and June, and $16,000.00 in September when I saw the year was runnin=
g ahead. Our 2025 return went in on October 13 with total tax of $59,302.33.

Attached are the full-year projection and the EFTPS history. The interim taxa=
ble income for the first three, six and nine months is in the folder; the win=
ter months were slow and the January 9 bonus to Celeste came out of Q1.

Two questions:
- How much should we pay on December 15, and are we short for the earlier qua=
rters?
- The EFTPS confirmation for the June 15 payment shows tax period 12/2025. I =
think I picked the wrong year. Does that matter?

Thanks,
Morgan Lee
Controller, HANGS Construction Services LLC

--=_HCS_2026_ES_request
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet
Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64
Content-Disposition: attachment;
 filename="2026 taxable income projection.xlsx"
